.TH CONNECT56 1 "2023-10-24" "CONNECT56 v2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
connect56 \- Cyber Security & Network Intelligence CLI Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./connect56.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITARGET\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CONNECT56
is an advanced Linux command\-line network intelligence and cyber security reconnaissance script.
It performs target inspection on IPv4, IPv6 addresses, or domain names to gather:
.IP \(bu 3
Target Resolution & Reverse DNS (PTR)
.IP \(bu 3
IP Geolocation, ASN Ownership & WHOIS/RDAP Registry details
.IP \(bu 3
BGP Routing Intelligence & RPKI validation status via RADB / RIPE Stat
.IP \(bu 3
DNS Record Enumeration (A, AAAA, NS, MX, TXT)
.IP \(bu 3
Web Reconnaissance (HTTP Status, Server Headers, Technology, Page Title)
.IP \(bu 3
Subdomain Enumeration & Health Monitoring (Categorized as ALIVE or DEAD based on DNS resolution)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output results as a structured JSON object suitable for SIEM, log aggregators, or automated pipelines.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color codes in output formatting.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-essential status messages and ASCII banners.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules \ \fIMODULES\fR
Specify intelligence modules to execute. \fIMODULES\fR can be a comma\-separated list of:
\fBall\fR, \fBwhois\fR, \fBdns\fR, \fBweb\fR, \fBsubdomain\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display script version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command usage guide and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
When executed without arguments in an interactive terminal session,
.B CONNECT56
will prompt the user to choose an intelligence module scan profile (1\-6).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ./connect56.sh 8.8.8.8
Run full reconnaissance scan against Google DNS IP address.
.TP
.B ./connect56.sh google.com \-\-json
Run full reconnaissance scan against google.com and return JSON format.
.TP
.B ./connect56.sh example.com \-m dns,subdomain
Run only DNS Enumeration and Subdomain Discovery against example.com.
.SH MANUAL INSTALLATION
To make \fBman connect56\fR available system\-wide:
.PP
.RS
sudo cp connect56.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
sudo mandb
.RE
